incant/derefAllT -- THE ** FIXPOINT UNWRAP.
Built 2026-09-01, Tony's ruling: keep ** as an operator and make its method
unwrap turtles all the way down.

WHY FIXPOINT AND NOT "TWICE"

"Exactly twice" was a guess at how deep the wrapping goes, and ANYtoken proves
the depth is not the reader's to know. "Unwrap until it stops unwrapping" is
depth-independent, which is what a reader downstream of a wrap-happy rule needs.

⚠ AND ** IS THE TOLERANT READER, NOT THE FIX FOR ANYtoken. The wart is the
producer's. ** only means no reader has to count its turtles.

THE THREE VERDICTS, as ruled

  V1 DEPTH 0 -- ** on a non-group returns it UNCHANGED. No error, where a
     single * refuses. So ** is TOTAL and IDEMPOTENT -- "normalize whatever
     this is". It follows that ** is NOT * iterated: the last step forgives
     what * refuses. Ruled, not inherited.
  V2 SPELLING -- one token, one meaning. `**x` is the fixpoint and differs from
     a single `*`. ⚠ THE SPACED FORM `* *x` IS NOT TESTED HERE BECAUSE IT
     CRASHES -- see the crash note below.
  V3 TERMINATION -- a depth cap with a squawk, 64 levels. Identity-at-definition
     probably forbids a group containing itself, but "probably" is not a guard,
     and one line turns a hang into a finding.

WHAT THIS FIXTURE PINS, AND IT IS NOT EVERYTHING

  R1  depth 0 is TOTAL          measured PLAIN, no error       V1
  R2  the control for R1        measured PLAIN                 anti-vacuity
  R3  the fixpoint at depth 1   measured LEAF                  the facility
  R4  `*x` differs from `**x`   measured 0 + error             V2

⚠ R2 IS NOT DECORATION. Without it R1 reading PLAIN is consistent with an
operator that does nothing at all to anything, which is exactly the shape rule
H4 forbids. The pair is the assertion; R1 alone is not.

⚠⚠ TWO OF CLAY'S CERTIFICATION LAWS ARE NOT PINNED HERE, AND THE REASON IS THE
FINDING RATHER THAN AN OMISSION

LAW 1, `**x == *x` on a single wrapper, WAS EXPECTED TO BE BUILDABLE AT DEPTH 1
AND IS NOT. Measured: `*daWrap` does not return LEAF, it ERRORS -- and the error
names daLeaf, not daWrap. So by the time unary * runs, the wrapper level has
ALREADY been consumed by runOP's auto-unwrap, and * is being handed the leaf.
The two sides of the law are therefore not comparable on this binary: ** reads
LEAF and * reads 0.

That is the same buildability problem Clay flagged for a depth-2 specimen,
ONE LEVEL LOWER THAN EXPECTED -- and it is also the plainest possible argument
FOR the fixpoint ruling, because it shows a reader cannot know what depth it is
handed even when it wrote the wrapper itself two lines earlier.

LAW 2, idempotence `**(**x) == **x`, HAS NO SPELLING THAT COMPOSES. `****x`
returns EMPTY, on a wrapped field and an unwrapped one alike, and `***x` errors
and returns empty. So repeated unary tokens do not compose into repeated
application, and the empty result is a fact about tokenising, NOT about
opDerefAll. Idempotence holds STRUCTURALLY -- the loop exits only when the
result is not a group, so a second application cannot enter the loop -- but that
is an argument, not a measurement, and it is labelled as one.

⚠ V2's REFUSAL CLAUSE IS UNIMPLEMENTED. Clay ruled `***x` should REFUSE. It does
not: it errors from the inner * and yields empty. Refusing by name needs
tokeniser work that was not in scope, and pinning the current behaviour would
freeze a wrong answer. Left unpinned and named here on purpose.

⚠⚠ AND A CRASH FOUND WHILE BUILDING THIS, BANKED AS docs/fixIts.md F-36:
`* *x` -- TWO SINGLE UNWRAPS, SPACE-SEPARATED -- TAKES THE PROCESS DOWN AT 139.

    ERROR Operator * failed on Token and xl1     then exit 139, no sentinel

It is NOT in this fixture, deliberately: rule H5 says a fixture must not be able
to delete the rest of the suite, and a crashing row would take every check below
it with no output to be suspicious of. R4 uses the single `*` instead, which
errors cleanly, returns 0, and lets the run continue.

⚠ THE FIRST PROBE THAT FOUND THE FIXPOINT ALSO DIED THIS WAY AND I READ IT AS A
CLEAN RUN, because the error line printed and I did not check for the sentinel.
Doctrine's own rule, walked into by the person applying it: absent sentinel means
the run truncated, and every "ok" above it is uninterpretable.

⚠ SO CLAY'S V2 IS NOT MERELY UNPINNED -- ITS PREMISE IS WRONG. The ruling reads
"a space means two single unwraps". Measured, a space means a CRASH. The
one-token/spaced distinction cannot be a spelling law until that is fixed.

